      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 952 and 365, I will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the multiplication**: We need to multiply 952 by 365. This means we are essentially adding 952 to itself 365 times.\n\n2. **Set up the multiplication**: We can use the standard algorithm for multiplication. This involves multiplying each digit of the first number (952) by each digit of the second number (365) and then adding the results.\n\n3. **Break down the multiplication**:\n   - First, multiply 952 by 5 (the units digit of 365).\n   - Then, multiply 952 by 60 (the tens digit of 365, which is 6 times 10).\n   - Finally, multiply 952 by 300 (the hundreds digit of 365, which is 3 times 100).\n\n4. **Perform the multiplications**:\n   - \\( 952 \\times 5 = 4760 \\)\n   - \\( 952 \\times 60 = 952 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 5712 \\times 10 = 57120 \\)\n   - \\( 952 \\times 300 = 952 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 2856 \\times 100 = 285600 \\)\n\n5. **Add the results**: Now, we add the three products together:\n   \\[\n   4760 + 57120 + 285600\n   \\]\n\n6. **Perform the addition**:\n   - First, add 4760 and 57120:\n     \\[\n     4760 + 57120 = 61880\n     \\]\n   - Next, add 61880 and 285600:\n     \\[\n     61880 + 285600 = 347480\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 952 and 365 is 347,480.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe product of 952 and 365 is 347,480.\n</answer>",
