      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 419 and 495, I will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the multiplication**: We need to multiply 419 by 495. This means we are essentially adding 419 to itself 495 times.\n\n2. **Set up the multiplication**: We can use the standard algorithm for multiplication, which involves breaking down the numbers and multiplying each part.\n\n3. **Break down the numbers**: \n   - 419 can be broken down into 400 + 10 + 9.\n   - 495 can be broken down into 400 + 90 + 5.\n\n4. **Multiply each part**:\n   - Multiply 419 by 400: \\(419 \\times 400 = 419 \\times 4 \\times 100 = 1676 \\times 100 = 167600\\).\n   - Multiply 419 by 90: \\(419 \\times 90 = 419 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 3771 \\times 10 = 37710\\).\n   - Multiply 419 by 5: \\(419 \\times 5 = 2095\\).\n\n5. **Add the results**: Now, we add the products of these multiplications together:\n   \\[\n   167600 + 37710 + 2095\n   \\]\n\n6. **Perform the addition**:\n   - First, add 167600 and 37710:\n     \\[\n     167600 + 37710 = 205310\n     \\]\n   - Next, add 205310 and 2095:\n     \\[\n     205310 + 2095 = 207405\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 419 and 495 is 207405.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe product of 419 and 495 is 207405.\n</answer>",
